% A Lightning to_local output (BOLT #3)
%
% The Logical English twin of a Bitcoin spending policy, written by the
% Miniscript translator. Who can spend the
% coin, when, and why: each rule is one spending path of the policy.
%
% Source: the Miniscript page
%         https://bitcoin.sipa.be/miniscript/
%
% The source, as written:
%     or(pk(key_revocation),and(pk(key_local),older(1008)))
%
% The source, laid out (keys and hashes by their role, <like this>):
%     or(
%       pk(<the revocation key>),
%       and(pk(<the local node>),older(1008)))
%
% The legend (role <- key or hash as written in the source):
%     the revocation key <- key_revocation
%     the local node     <- key_local
%
% What it says (the spending policy, by BIP 379's semantics):
%     any one of these:
%       a signature by the revocation key
%       all of these:
%         a signature by the local node
%         the coin at least 1008 blocks old (about 7 days; older(1008))
%
% Try it in Minsc (the policy compiled to Miniscript, Script and an address,
% in the browser): the document "the policy in Minsc" below.
%
% DISCLAIMER. This program was written by a translator from a program of another
% system. It is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or
% implied, including any warranty that it is accurate, complete or fit for a
% particular purpose. The translation may be wrong: check it against its source
% before relying on it. It is not legal, tax, insurance, financial or other
% professional advice. Its authors accept no liability for any loss or damage
% arising from its use.

the target language is: prolog.

the knowledge base bolt3_to_local includes these resources:
    temporal.

the templates are:
    the coin can be spent.
    the coin was confirmed in block *a height*; scenario element.
    the spending transaction is in block *a height*; scenario element.
    the coin has been confirmed for *a number* blocks.
    the witness contains a signature by *a key*; scenario element.

the knowledge base bolt3_to_local includes:

the Miniscript page is published at "https://bitcoin.sipa.be/miniscript/".
the text of the Miniscript page is at "sources/sipa_miniscript.txt".

the policy in Minsc is published at "https://min.sc/#c=//%20A%20Lightning%20to_local%20output%20(BOLT%20%233)%0A//%20The%20Logical%20English%20twin's%20policy%20(the%20Miniscript%20translator%20of%20Logical%20English).%0A$revocation_key%20=%20028071f961bf66967e8b92b2564cca5590e958305ce382ebeeb56e866b6baf3edc;%20%20%20//%20the%20revocation%20key%20(a%20test%20key:%20the%20source%20names%20no%20key)%0A$local_node%20=%20038fed93f74b169ba9410f1a39dde6b9c6eea84650dc79967a27f52757c197fbc8;%20%20%20//%20the%20local%20node%20(a%20test%20key:%20the%20source%20names%20no%20key)%0A%0Aor(pk($revocation_key),and(pk($local_node),older(1008)))%0A".

the Tape run of 2026-09-14 is published at "https://tape.rewindbitcoin.com/explorer/address/bcrt1qgkt0u8lhwq5spjrvljrsdc02lmjzxh970jnr9jqycq0zrzxrxfcsh28204".
the text of the Tape run of 2026-09-14 is at "sources/bolt3_to_local.chain.json".

% The spending paths of the policy.
rule revocation with provenance the Miniscript page,
        confer "The BOLT #3 to_local policy: or(pk(key_revocation),and(pk(key_local),older(1008)))":
the coin can be spent if
    the witness contains a signature by the revocation key.

rule local_after_delay with provenance the Miniscript page,
        confer "The BOLT #3 to_local policy: or(pk(key_revocation),and(pk(key_local),older(1008)))":
the coin can be spent if
    the witness contains a signature by the local node
    and the coin has been confirmed for a number N blocks
    and N >= 1008.

% The age of the coin, which the relative timelocks (older) measure.
rule coin_age_in_blocks:
the coin has been confirmed for a number N blocks if
    the coin was confirmed in block a height H
    and the spending transaction is in block a height M
    and N = M - H.

scenario local_after_delay is, as stated in the satisfaction analysis of the policy:
    % spending path local_after_delay — the path needs: a coin 1008 blocks old, a signature by the local node
    the witness contains a signature by the local node.
    the coin was confirmed in block 850000.
    the spending transaction is in block 851008.
    spendable expects answers ["the coin can be spent"].

